{"term":"concern","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:f5ad8d749fb6219e82","definition":"That which affects one’s welfare or happiness. A matter of interest to someone.","example":"Mark’s health was of great concern to Connie.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["interest"],"antonyms":["unconcern"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["book concern","concern group","concernment","concern troll","concernworthy","dual-use research of concern","microconcern","misconcern","nonconcern","separation of concerns","unconcernment","underconcern","overconcern"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concern#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:734cf0406d08154785","definition":"The placement of interest or worry on a subject.","example":"Most people in Australia have no concern for the recent events in London.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["book concern","concern group","concernment","concern troll","concernworthy","dual-use research of concern","microconcern","misconcern","nonconcern","separation of concerns","unconcernment","underconcern","overconcern"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concern#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ea055e8b9d5ae339a7","definition":"A worry; a sense that something may be wrong; an identification of a possible problem.","example":"Let me know if you have any questions or concerns about the document.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["book concern","concern group","concernment","concern troll","concernworthy","dual-use research of concern","microconcern","misconcern","nonconcern","separation of concerns","unconcernment","underconcer